            <div xml:id="d30">

                <pb facs="0136" n="16" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg16"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.6363/1117</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-26">March 26, 1931</date>.<lb/>[Received April
                        15.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2381</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my despatch No. 2376 of March
                    24 (File No. 801.A Rublee), in which I spoke of the excellent work which had <pb
                        facs="0137" n="17" xml:id="pg17"/> been done here by Mr. Rublee, I have the
                    honor to report that President Olaya took the occasion yesterday to ask me to
                    express to the Department of State his appreciation of what Mr. Rublee had done.
                    He said that Mr. Rublee had been “more than satisfactory;” the Government was
                    delighted with what he had done, both in connection with the oil law and in
                    connection with the signing of the Barco contract.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
